      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "THIS IS CLIP 1 (the initial generation)\n---------------------------------------\nSave Latent writes the AV latent to\n  ComfyUI/output/h3_latents/<name>_00001.h3latent.safetensors\n\nThen, in the continuation workflow:\n  1. Un-bypass Load Latent (Ctrl+B)\n  2. Pick that file (newest is at the top)\n  3. Write the next prompt and run\n\n-- continuing from the VIDEO costs a decode plus a\nre-encode, which darkens the picture about 2.4% per clip and\ncompounds. But Continuing from the LATENT skips that entirely.\n\nIMPORTANT: note this clip's width and height. Every continuation\nmust use the same ones. A latent cannot be resized, and the\nResolution preset is a pixel budget, not a fixed frame size, so\nthe same preset at a different aspect ratio will not match."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "THIS IS CLIP 1 (the initial generation)\n---------------------------------------\nSave Latent writes the AV latent to\n  ComfyUI/output/h3_latents/<name>_00001.h3latent.safetensors\n\nThen, in the continuation workflow:\n  1. Un-bypass Load Latent (Ctrl+B)\n  2. Pick that file (newest is at the top)\n  3. Write the next prompt and run\n\n-- continuing from the VIDEO costs a decode plus a\nre-encode, which darkens the picture about 2.4% per clip and\ncompounds. But Continuing from the LATENT skips that entirely.\n\nIMPORTANT: note this clip's width and height. Every continuation\nmust use the same ones. A latent cannot be resized, and the\nResolution preset is a pixel budget, not a fixed frame size, so\nthe same preset at a different aspect ratio will not match."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
